Track 2: Sluice-Gate Protocol
- Story & Context: Maren, the band's percussionist, hides her secret map of the old transit tunnels inside the hollow cavity of her rhythm-pad cabinet. She confessed to the band that she heard the accelerator whispering about a "sub-harmonic tide" during the midnight session. "Does the rusted valve ever turn the light?" she asks, knowing that opening the main gate will likely implode the dancefloor.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A close-up of a rusted iron sluice-gate door being pried open by a hand adorned with copper wires, emitting a blinding, unnatural violet geometric light, dark, moody photography style.

Track 3: Anchoring The Ghost-Particle
- Story & Context: Years after the site was sealed, the locals at the surface recount the night the building hummed for forty-eight hours straight, long after the last dancer had left. The myth holds that Elias trapped a fragment of a lost particle within a custom loop-pedal, and it continues to cycle through his last composition. "Leave the anchor in the wreckage," they chant at the harbor, watching the lights in the derelict tower flicker in time to an impossible, phantom rhythm.
